.TH EQN 1
.SH NAME
eqn \- typeset mathematics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eqn
[
.BI -c " chars"
] [
.B -t
] [
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Eqn
is a preprocessor for
.IR troff (1):
it reads troff's input from the
.IR file s,
in order
.RB ( -
its standard input), or from its standard input if none is named, and
writes it on its standard output with each equation turned into what
troff sets it by
(Neateqn reads only its standard input, and named no file;
.B "eqn /lib/troff/eqnrc -"
reads the settings first, then the document).
An equation is a display, between
.B .EQ
and
.BR .EN ,
or within a line, between the two characters a
.B delim
statement names:
.IP
.EX
\&.EQ
delim $$
\&.EN
The sum $sum from i=1 to n x sub i$ and its mean $x bar$.
\&.EQ
int from 0 to inf e sup {-x sup 2} dx = {sqrt pi} over 2
\&.EN
.EE
.PP
Its language is Kernighan and Cherry's
.RB ( sub ,
.BR sup ,
.BR over ,
.BR sqrt ,
.BR from ,
.BR to ,
.BR left ,
.BR right ,
.BR pile ,
.BR matrix ,
.BR define
and the rest), set by TeX's rules for mathematics, as Ali Gholami Rudi's
Neateqn sets it, of which
.I eqn
is a translation; for the same input its output is, byte for byte,
Neateqn's.
.B /lib/troff/eqnrc
gives it Libertinus Math: its brackets, radicals and operators in the
sizes the font has for them, its own parameters (its MATH table's: the
sizes of scripts, the shifts of scripts, numerators and denominators,
the axis, the rules), the names of functions as operators, an
integral's limits beside it;
.IR book (1)
reads it first.
.PP
Beyond Neateqn:
.B "set script_percent_scale_down"
.I n
and
.B "set script_script_percent_scale_down"
.I n
make scripts, and their scripts,
.I n
per cent of the text's size (not each 7/10 of the one above);
.BI nolimits " x"
sets the
.B from
and
.B to
of the operator
.I x
as its scripts, beside it, as TeX's
.BR \enolimits ;
.B "set tex_script_drop 1"
raises a script on a single character from its baseline, and drops one
on a larger base by the script's size, as TeX's rule 18a (not from
every base's top, in the base's size);
.B "set fraction_display_gap"
.I n
and
.B "set fraction_gap"
.I n
are the least gaps between a fraction's bar and its numerator or
denominator, displayed and in text, in hundredths of an em (the font's
.B FractionNumDisplayStyleGapMin
and
.BR FractionNumeratorGapMin ).
.PP
Beyond Neateqn too, in its language:
.B "root"
.I "n x"
sets the
.IR n th
root of
.IR x ,
its degree in scriptscript style, raised and kerned into the radical
by the font's parameters (TeX's
.BR \esqrt[n]{x} );
.B overbrace
.I x
and
.B underbrace
.I x
set a brace over or under
.IR x ,
the font's own sizes or one made of its pieces, the whole a big
operator, so that
.B to
(or
.BR from )
puts a label over (or under) it;
.B displaystyle
and
.B textstyle
set what follows in a display's or text's style
.RB ( \edfrac ,
.BR \ecfrac );
.B "type op icorr"
.I n
gives an operator its italic correction, in hundredths of an em, for
its subscript to sit under its tail, as TeX sets an integral's;
.B gsfont
.I f
sets operators, relations and punctuation in the font
.I f
(the math font's, as TeX's), not
.BR grfont 's.
.PP
And these settings, each 0 (Neateqn's way) unless set, as
.B /lib/troff/eqnrc
sets them:
.B "set tex_arrays 1"
sets a matrix as TeX sets an array, each column its own width, each row
its own height and depth (a strut's at least), the whole centred on the
axis;
.B "set tex_atoms 1"
makes
.B {}
an ordinary atom and keeps a relation at a box's start a relation, so
that
.B "{} = 0"
is spaced as TeX's, and makes
.B left
\&...
.B right
one inner atom;
.B "set tex_greek 1"
sets capital Greek upright;
.B "set fraction_ord 1"
makes a fraction an ordinary atom, as LaTeX's
.B \efrac
(braced) is, no thin space beside it;
.B "set math_italic 1"
sets letters in roman italic as the math font's maths italic
(a to U+1D44E, A to U+1D434, h to U+210E, Greek to U+1D6FC on), as TeX's
.BR unicode-math ,
each letter's italic correction after it (but before its scripts);
.B "set tex_accents 1"
sets
.BR hat ,
.BR tilde ,
.BR bar ,
.BR dot ,
.BR dotdot ,
.B vec
and
.B dyad
as TeX's, from the math font's glyphs that
.B accent
.I "name n glyph pos width"
\&... gives (the first the accent's, the rest its wider variants), its
attachment on the base glyph's that
.B accentpos
.I "n glyph pos"
\&... gives (or the middle of what is under it), raised by what that
passes
.B "set accent_base_height"
.IR n ,
in thousandths of an em but the height; over more than one glyph the
widest variant not wider than it, and
.B bar
an overline;
.B "set tex_fractions 1"
sets a fraction's numerator and denominator in TeX's styles for them
(in text style in script size, in a script in scriptscript size);
.B "set script_kern"
.I n
is the kern before scripts (Neateqn's 5);
.BR "set sub_superscript_gap_min" ,
.BR superscript_bottom_max_with_subscript ,
.B superscript_bottom_min
and
.B subscript_top_max
are the font's limits on scripts;
.BR "set radical_vertical_gap" ,
.BR radical_display_vertical_gap ,
.BR radical_rule_thickness ,
.BR radical_degree_bottom_raise_percent ,
.B radical_kern_before_degree
and
.B radical_kern_after_degree
its radicals';
.B "set delimiter_factor"
.I n
and
.B "set delimiter_shortfall"
.I n
size a delimiter as TeX's
.B \edelimiterfactor
and
.BR \edelimitershortfall ;
.B "set stretch_stack_gap"
.I n
is a brace's gap from what it is over or under.
All are in hundredths of an em but the percentages and the factor.
.TP
.BI -c " chars"
The characters an equation within a line may be broken after.
.TP
.B -t
Each equation a
.B Formula
for a tagged PDF
.RI ( tr2pdf (1)),
described by its eqn, as written; a display a block of its own.
The output is then no longer Neateqn's.
.SH FILES
.B /lib/troff/eqnrc
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/eqn
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR book (1),
.IR troff (1)
.br
B. W. Kernighan and L. L. Cherry,
\(lqA System for Typesetting Mathematics\(rq,
